<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Telugu strings of the iPhone UI. values/strings.xml has the comments for each key: where the text shows,
  the placeholders and the length limits. docs/LOCALIZATION_GLOSSARY.md gives the terms and their sources.
  The polite form "మీరు" with "-ండి", and English loanwords where Telugu iOS uses them ("సేవ్", "డిలీట్", "ఎడిట్").
  Telugu has the CLDR plural forms one and other. Labels with 16 characters say "నొప్పిలేని రోజు" (pain-free day) in the singular.
  The Export tab is "ఎగుమతి", because "ఎక్స్‌పోర్ట్" is longer than 10 characters. The duration chips have no unit.
-->
